<Prose
  title="Shipping"
  description="Dispatch times, shipping rates and delivery for PB&B orders."
  heading="Shipping"
  standfirst="Rates and delivery estimates are calculated at checkout once your address is known."
  updated="[CONFIRM] date"
>
  <h2>Dispatch</h2>
  <p>
    Orders are packed and dispatched within <mark class="todo">[CONFIRM] 2 business days</mark>.
    You'll get a tracking number by email as soon as the label is created. Orders placed on a
    weekend or a public holiday go out on the next business day.
  </p>

  <h2>Rates</h2>
  <p>
    Live rates are shown at checkout based on your address and the weight of the order — nothing is
    marked up beyond the carrier's price.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Free US shipping</strong> on orders over <mark class="todo">[CONFIRM] $150</mark>.</li>
    <li><strong>US standard</strong> — <mark class="todo">[CONFIRM] rate and carrier</mark>.</li>
    <li><strong>US expedited</strong> — <mark class="todo">[CONFIRM] rate and carrier</mark>.</li>
    <li><strong>International</strong> — <mark class="todo">[CONFIRM] destinations and rates</mark>.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <mark class="todo">[CONFIRM]</mark> Which shipping zones are configured in Shopify. Rates will
    not calculate at checkout for any zone that has not been set up, and the order will fail — this
    is worth testing per destination before launch.
  </p>

  <h2>Delivery estimates</h2>
  <p>
    <mark class="todo">[CONFIRM] Transit times per service.</mark> These are carrier estimates and
    not guarantees; once a parcel is scanned in, its progress is out of our hands.
  </p>

  <h2>Duties and import charges</h2>
  <p>
    <mark class="todo">[CONFIRM]</mark> Whether international prices include duties, or whether the
    recipient pays them on delivery. Getting this wrong is the most common cause of refused
    international parcels, so it should be stated plainly.
  </p>

  <h2>Wrong address</h2>
  <p>
    Check your address at checkout. If you spot a mistake, email
    <a href="/contact">support</a> straight away — we can usually correct it before dispatch, but
    once a parcel has shipped we can't reroute it.
  </p>

  <h2>Lost or damaged parcels</h2>
  <p>
    If tracking stalls for more than <mark class="todo">[CONFIRM] 10 business days</mark>, or your
    order arrives damaged, contact us with your order number and we'll open a claim with the carrier
    and sort you out. You do not have to deal with the carrier yourself.
  </p>
</Prose>
